WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.900
Treasure Island

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:14.990
Hey, Old Redruth?

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.660
Ye, what is it?

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.020
Is it much further?

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:22.090
Well, I'd say we're stuck halfway
between home and Bristol.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.100
Hey, what's wrong?

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.220
Are you thinking of your little mother that you left at Black Hill?

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.260
You kidding?
Not at all!

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:43.310
<i>Have a nice trip, Jim!
And don't worry about me!</i>

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:47.730
<i>Every man dreams of going out to sea.</i>

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.180
<i>Go on, Jim.
Your ship is waiting in Bristol.</i>

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>Go on, Jim.</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.210
<i>Do your best to behave like a man.</i>

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:06.960
Hey, Jim you see that?

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.180
That's the port of Bristol!

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.960
Treasure
Island

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.760
Takarajima

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:34.570
saa ikou

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:34.570
Come, let's go

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.660
yume ni mita shima heto

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.660
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:41.500
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:41.500
Across the waves, on the wind

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:44.380
umi hedeyou

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:44.380
We'll travel the oceans

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.300
ikute ni wa

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.300
Many of us

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:50.300
minna mada shiranai

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:50.300
Still don't know of

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:54.050
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:54.050
The days and nights full of mystery

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.550
matte iru darou

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.550
That await us there

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.060
itsumo shinji you

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.060
We must always have trust

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.310
magokoro wo

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.310
And be sincere

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:09.570
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:09.570
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:12.700
tade hitotsu no

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:12.700
I only...

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:16.120
akogare dake wa

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:16.120
...have one desire

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:18.410
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:18.410
And no one...

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:25.120
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:25.120
...will ever take it away

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.670
tade hitotsu no

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.670
I only...

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.970
akogare dake wa

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.970
...have one desire

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.300
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.300
And no one...

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:44.230
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:44.230
...will ever take it away

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:55.110
episode

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:55.110
John Silver;
\h      Friend or foe?

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:18.080
Say, old man, where is our ship,
the Hispaniola?

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:21.800
You can't see it from here.
This port is crowded, you see.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.600
Most of the ships are anchored offshore.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:42.910
Damn it...

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:44.680
Mom packed it to the brim.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:46.480
I can't carry it anymore.

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.080
Baggagers, if you please!

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:51.420
Don't just stand there.
Take my things to my room!

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.880
Which room is it, anyway—

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:59.090
You finally came.
We were waiting for you, Jim.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:01.970
Dr. Livesey!
Mr. Trelawney!

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.890
Yes, I've finally arrived!

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:13.320
Jim, your father was a childhood friend of Dr. Livesey and I.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:16.160
But on the ship, work is work,

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.860
Do not expect any favouritism from us.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.650
Right, I understand.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:27.640
Jim, I've decided to entrust you with the position of cabin boy.

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:28.830
I'm counting on you.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.600
Yes, sir!
I will do my best.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:33.720
By the way, when do we depart?

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:34.710
Tomorrow.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:35.630
Really, tomorrow?

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.880
If the sky and the wind are in our favour.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:45.680
It's all right.
It will be beautiful, I assure you!

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:49.080
So, you know the sea winds, Jim?

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:52.720
Obviously. At Black Hill,
I watched the sea everyday.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.710
You know that, Mr. Trelawney!

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:58.560
Without further ado,
I'll give you your first job.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.480
Yes, Captain Trelawney!

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:03.800
Just a second, my young friend.
I'm not the captain.

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:05.560
What must I call you then?

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:07.200
Well, I am...

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.000
A position more important than captain.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.920
You see, I am the shipowner.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:14.480
Yes, understood, owner Trelawney!

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:22.430
So, owner Trelawney,
about that urgent errand?

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:24.010
Oh yes, that's right.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:28.640
I want you to take this to
the landlord of the Spyglass.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:29.350
Understood.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:31.940
Count on me, owner Trelawney.

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:34.270
Come on, Benbow!

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:40.520
What energy. He didn't even ask where to find the tavern.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:44.200
Redruth, catch up with him and tell him the way.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:45.370
Very well.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.530
E-Excuse me,

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:52.540
by landlord of the tavern...

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:54.000
Do you mean the one-legged man?

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:01.160
It's time to make things clear, Jim.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:04.520
This isn't the same one-legged man!

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:07.940
He isn't the one that Billy Bones feared.

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:10.010
It's another man!
You don't have to worry.

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:12.970
Moreover, Jim.

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:18.230
We were able to prepare our quick departure mostly because of him.

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:23.960
I'll have you know, when I talked to him about you, he told me he had to meet you right away.

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:25.350
Could you tell me his name?

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:28.670
It's Silver.
Yes, John Silver.

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:31.120
John Silver, huh?

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:38.730
Let's see... At the fountain,
you must turn right.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:49.380
<i>That damn one-legged man.</i>

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:51.980
<i>The one I fear has one leg!</i>

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:56.590
<i>After Black Dog, he sends Blind Pew to kill me.</i>

00:06:56.590 --> 00:06:59.550
<i>Yes, it's him behind it all!</i>

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:01.850
<i>Damn it! It's him!</i>

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:04.740
<i>It's that damn one-legged man!</i>

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:18.330
<i>I must get to the bottom of this!</i>

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:22.290
<i>Is John Silver the famous
one-legged man or isn't he?</i>

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:36.640
The Spyglass tavern...

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:38.600
All right.
Let's go, Benbow.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:45.060
Wh-What's the matter, Benbow?

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:48.690
B-Benbow, let go of me.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:02.210
It's Black Dog...

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:14.760
He went into the tavern.

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:18.430
<i>It's the one-legged man that I'm looking for!</i>

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:22.730
<i>He was the one hiding behind Black Dog and Blind Pew!</i>

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:27.190
No doubt about it! The landlord is the famous one-legged man!

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:43.940
I knew they had been fooled!
Dr. Livesey and Mr. Trelawney alike!

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:45.460
I have to do <i>something!</i>

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:51.460
But what <i>can</i> I do?
I need indisputable evidence!

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:05.730
Tell me, kid. Is my tavern interesting to you?

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:22.610
Kid, is my tavern interesting to you?
My tavern! Kid!

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:28.130
You're John Silver, aren't you?

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:30.920
That's right.
And you?

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:33.310
I am Jim.
Jim Hawkins.

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:36.930
Here, Mr. Trelawney asked me
to bring you this note.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:43.590
Oh, that's right.
You are Jim, the new cabin boy?

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:44.550
That's right.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:48.860
As for me, I was hired as the
master cook for this voyage.

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:50.840
Nice to meet you.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:51.590
Have a nice day!

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:52.340
Have a nice day!

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:53.090
Have a nice day!

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:53.910
Have a nice day!

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:55.260
Have a nice day!

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:56.280
Have a nice day!

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:02.370
I'm counting on you.

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:03.690
Have a nice day!

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:04.350
Have a nice day!

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:05.270
Have a nice day!

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:05.940
Have a nice day!

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:06.610
Have a nice day!

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:07.570
Have a nice day!

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:08.370
Have a nice day!

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:12.090
Now, don't stay out here.
Come talk inside.

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:19.310
<i>He won't have me fooled so easily!</i>

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:24.140
Blind Pew is dead!

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:32.170
Blind... Pew?

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:34.570
That's an uncommon name.
Who is that?

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:38.530
Black Dog! Black! Black I tell you!
You know him, don't you?!

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:43.630
Yes, I know "Black".
It's the dog of the port's barber.

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:45.490
Has something happened to him?

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:47.960
Stop playing innocent!

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:51.000
I've seen him!
Black Dog went into your tavern!

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:54.000
He's one of the pirates
that attacked Billy Bones!

00:10:54.390 --> 00:10:57.720
And I just saw him enter your tavern!

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:08.520
Are you running away, John Silver?!

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:31.350
Silver! Silver! Silver!
John Silver!

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:33.040
John Silver!

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:36.350
Billy. Billy! Billy.

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:46.220
Where is Black Dog?

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:52.310
Where is the pirate who dared to come
drink in this respectable establishment?

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:55.020
Is it you?!

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:56.690
No, not at all!

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:58.170
So, is it you?!

00:11:58.170 --> 00:11:59.490
Wh-Who me?!

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:06.740
Is it you?

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:07.950
Shut up!

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:10.660
Wait, you bastard!

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:11.710
Let's go, Benbow!

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:25.720
I'm done for!

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:36.070
Jim, are you sure that this man is Black Dog?

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:39.750
Yes, no doubt!
It's him who attacked our inn!

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:41.530
He even tried to kill me!

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:44.450
Okay, okay...

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:47.200
Then I'll have to teach him a lesson.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:49.350
For trying to kill Jim...

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:54.020
...and for daring to show your ugly
pirate mug and drink my good rum.

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:56.150
Stay back!

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:13.230
I think I went a little too hard on him.

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:17.980
Jim, what should we do?
Should we call the police?

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:20.230
Silver, behind you!

00:13:37.310 --> 00:13:40.200
Damn it!
Y-You'll pay for this!

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:45.270
That guy really barks like a dog.

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:50.890
So Jim, you see now that I'm not one of them?

00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:56.730
Looks like you still doubt me.

00:13:57.340 --> 00:14:00.470
But I guess that's okay.
Trusting someone too quickly...

00:14:00.470 --> 00:14:02.520
...isn't a very smart thing to do.

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:10.950
That's right, it was my crutch that stopped his sword.

00:14:16.150 --> 00:14:19.180
What's wrong?
Can't you walk any faster?

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:31.550
What's with the glare?

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:37.410
Lean on my shoulder.

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:38.860
Don't worry about me!

00:14:39.670 --> 00:14:41.550
The tavern is just around the corner.

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:45.440
There, I have a lot of spare crutches waiting for me.

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:55.580
Enough already, I believe you.
Lean on me.

00:14:58.950 --> 00:15:02.130
I'm sorry, Jim.
It's our first meeting...

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.540
...and I'm already asking for your help.

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:08.470
Anyway, at sea I must help you.

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.220
I'm counting on you, "matey".

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:13.280
Here you go.

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:17.020
W-Wait...
I didn't order beer.

00:15:17.710 --> 00:15:19.870
Don't worry, it's my treat.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:23.500
Come, drink with me, Jim.
We will celebrate our meeting.

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:25.740
O-Okay...

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:31.590
Hey, Jim, you've never drank alcohol?

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:34.750
You've gotta be kidding!
I also run an inn!

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:38.670
I drink to pass the time, but my mother doesn't know it!

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:39.540
Alright, let's go!

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:41.040
Cheers!

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:42.520
Cheers!

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:50.060
<i>In reality, it was the first time in my life that I drank alcohol.</i>

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:05.610
Go on, kill me!
I don't care!

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:09.530
You lookin' for me?
You asked for it!

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:12.390
Sorry, Jim.
It's all my fault.

00:16:12.390 --> 00:16:14.830
If I had known you could not stand alcohol,

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:16.670
I wouldn't have given it to you.

00:16:16.670 --> 00:16:20.030
Shut up! If we can't get drunk at 13 years, when will we?

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:23.430
What? 13...
You're only 13 years old?

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:27.930
Heavens, I made a child drink.
Shame on you, Silver.

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:29.220
I'm really sorry.

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:35.350
Come, Jim.
You must return to the inn...

00:16:35.350 --> 00:16:37.590
...or Mr. Trelawney and his friends will worry.

00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:39.680
Just leave me alone...

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:41.270
Come, Jim.

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:54.390
<i>"Dear mother, how are you?"</i>

00:16:54.390 --> 00:16:57.320
<i>"I'm doing well.
Very well even!"</i>

00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:03.280
<i>"Actually, today I met the one-legged landlord of a tavern by the name of John Silver."</i>

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:09.210
<i>"And at first, I thought that he was
Billy Bone's one-legged man, but now..."</i>

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:11.920
<i>"I was wrong, completely wrong!"</i>

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:14.960
<i>"Silver smells like the sea."</i>

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:17.510
<i>"The smell of sailors like Dad."</i>

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:22.030
<i>"From the Bristol hotel I can see the stars shining."</i>

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:26.220
<i>"Signed, your son, Jim Hawkins,
on the eve of departure."</i>

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:39.870
Look, Jim.
It's our ship, the Hispaniola.

00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:56.930
Hey, guys! The shipowner and his friends have arrived!

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:10.480
Mr. Trelawney, we were waiting for you.

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:15.570
We've been on board since last night.
Everything is ready for departure.

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.650
Yes, good work.
Let me introduce you.

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:20.620
I present to you our cabin boy, Jim Hawkins.

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:24.690
Nice to meet you, Jim.
I am Arrow, the first mate.

00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:26.250
Mr. Trelawney.

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:31.960
Hello, Captain Smollett.
We're in luck.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:34.310
It's the perfect day to cast off.

00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:36.550
Thank heavens.

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:38.930
I want to talk to you, Mr. Trelawney.

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:41.260
What?
Oh, sure...

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:43.850
Alright then, let's go to my cabin.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:52.020
See ya later, Jim!

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:52.520
Bye!

00:18:53.090 --> 00:18:57.490
So, Captain Smollett, what did you want to talk to me about?

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:01.750
If I may, I'm going to speak honestly, sir.

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:04.740
This voyage means nothing to me!

00:19:06.650 --> 00:19:07.680
What's that?!

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:09.490
The crew doesn't please me.

00:19:09.490 --> 00:19:10.960
And neither does my first mate.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:13.170
Wait a minute, Smollett.

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:15.650
The reason I hired Mr. Arrow as First Mate,

00:19:15.650 --> 00:19:19.510
was because he was recommended to me
by the Admiralty, just like you.

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:22.640
Although he has a position of high responsibility,

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.970
Arrow is too close to the crew.

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:27.410
I don't see anything wrong with that.

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:29.250
Silver chose half of them.

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:31.830
The others had letters of recommendation—

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:33.690
Additionally, my employer does not please me either!

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:34.690
Wh-Wha?!

00:19:36.010 --> 00:19:38.650
Shouldn't the purpose of this voyage be classified?

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:40.360
That goes without saying.

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:44.570
Only Mr. Trelawney, Jim and I know of it.

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:46.490
So, where is the problem?

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:50.170
The problem is that rumours are circling amongst the crew:

00:19:50.170 --> 00:19:52.240
"We're going after treasure!"

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:54.880
"We are searching for
Great Pirate Flint's treasure!"

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:56.340
That's what they say!

00:19:58.410 --> 00:19:59.720
Mr. Trelawney.

00:20:00.850 --> 00:20:03.970
I think someone has been too talkative.

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:08.570
Let me see. The last time I had a drink was with Silver,

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:11.170
Arrow and quarter master Hands...

00:20:11.170 --> 00:20:13.940
I only talked with those three!

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:16.730
So it really was you.

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:18.840
And just what is wrong with that?

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:21.400
Master is the shipowner, right?

00:20:21.770 --> 00:20:25.370
Once at sea, the captain is the only one responsible.

00:20:26.010 --> 00:20:29.570
I do not care about your stories of treasure.
I don't want to know!

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:33.770
But if gold fever takes over crew,
they will be uncontrollable!

00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:35.130
Understand?

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:38.850
Shipowner or not, you must watch your tongue!

00:20:38.850 --> 00:20:42.410
If you can't do that,
 then I'd rather leave this ship!

00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:45.180
What?
You insolent...!

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:46.730
Easy now, Mr. Trelawney...

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:49.010
Understood.
We will do as you say.

00:20:49.410 --> 00:20:53.570
From now on, we will try to be more cautious. Alright?

00:20:53.570 --> 00:20:56.700
I have no complaints if you understand.
Now, excuse me.

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:03.820
Hey, you!
What are you doing there?!

00:21:05.190 --> 00:21:07.680
You woke me, Captain.
I'm sorry...

00:21:07.680 --> 00:21:09.810
I was about to get some shut-eye.

00:21:10.610 --> 00:21:14.710
I'm the lookout boy, Puppy "the seagull".
Nice to meet you.

00:21:15.090 --> 00:21:17.670
Return to your post!
We will raise the anchor!

00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:20.100
Yes, very well.
I will go.

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:30.890
Raise the anchor!

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:33.850
Deploy the sails!
Forward!

00:22:20.610 --> 00:22:23.120
<i>Here I am, finally at sea!</i>

00:22:23.120 --> 00:22:25.530
<i>Setting off for Treasure Island!</i>

00:22:25.530 --> 00:22:27.710
<i>I... I... I am...!</i>

00:22:27.710 --> 00:22:29.160
<i>Mother, I really am!</i>

00:22:28.540 --> 00:22:32.370
To      be        continued

00:22:30.420 --> 00:22:32.370
<i>Huzzah!</i>

00:22:33.370 --> 00:22:38.410
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:33.370 --> 00:22:38.410
Hey sea breeze

00:22:38.410 --> 00:22:44.220
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:38.410 --> 00:22:44.220
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:45.440 --> 00:22:50.430
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:45.440 --> 00:22:50.430
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:50.430 --> 00:22:55.870
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:50.430 --> 00:22:55.870
A word to my dear mother

00:22:55.870 --> 00:23:01.280
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:55.870 --> 00:23:01.280
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:01.280 --> 00:23:06.740
kaban ippai no

00:23:01.280 --> 00:23:06.740
And that my bag filled

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:12.370
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:12.370
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:18.230
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:18.230
Will be brought back

00:23:19.320 --> 00:23:24.820
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:19.320 --> 00:23:24.820
The sunset on my back

00:23:24.820 --> 00:23:30.710
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:24.820 --> 00:23:30.710
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:30.710 --> 00:23:40.430
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:30.710 --> 00:23:40.430
I blow out a whistle

00:23:45.170 --> 00:23:47.370
There isn't a puff of wind.

00:23:47.370 --> 00:23:49.410
Our Hispaniola has stopped.

00:23:49.410 --> 00:23:52.740
The heat is stifling and the crew picks a fight with me.

00:23:53.170 --> 00:23:55.490
Luckily, Silver gets me out of trouble.

00:23:55.490 --> 00:23:59.120
He invites me to procure dinner for the crew.

00:23:59.450 --> 00:24:03.130
What can be caught with a harpoon in the Atlantic?

00:24:03.130 --> 00:24:04.670
A big whale?

00:24:05.490 --> 00:24:08.670
Next time on Treasure Island:
"Ol' Barbecue is a Tough Guy"

00:24:08.670 --> 00:24:09.730
Don't miss it!

00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:13.680
m 0 0 l 960 0 960 720 0 720

00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:13.680
*

00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:13.680
Next time

00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:13.680
Coming soon!

00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:13.680
Ol ' Barbecue
is a Tough Guy
